statement:
A cat and a mouse play on the board `grid`, an array of equal-length strings. Each cell is a wall `'#'`, open floor `'.'`, the food `'F'`, the cat's starting cell `'C'` or the mouse's starting cell `'M'`. Each of `'C'`, `'M'` and `'F'` appears exactly once, and those three cells are walkable like floor.

The mouse moves first, then the two alternate. On its turn a player either stays where it is or picks one of the four directions (up, down, left, right) and slides in a straight line by any number of cells from 1 up to its limit: `mouseJump` for the mouse, `catJump` for the cat. A move may not leave the board and may not enter or cross a wall. The mouse is allowed to pass over the cat's cell.

The game stops at the first of these events:

- the cat and the mouse are on the same cell: the cat wins;
- the cat gets to the food before the mouse does: the cat wins;
- the mouse gets to the food before the cat does: the mouse wins;
- the mouse has not reached the food within 1000 turns: the cat wins.

Assuming both play optimally, return `true` if the mouse wins and `false` otherwise.

validator:
function validate([grid, catJump, mouseJump]) {
  if (!Array.isArray(grid) || grid.length < 1 || grid.length > 8) return 'grid needs 1 to 8 rows.';
  const cols = grid[0].length;
  if (cols < 1 || cols > 8) return 'Each row needs 1 to 8 cells.';
  if (grid.some(row => typeof row !== 'string' || row.length !== cols)) return 'All rows must have the same length.';
  if (grid.some(row => /[^CMF.#]/.test(row))) return "Cells may only be 'C', 'M', 'F', '.' or '#'.";
  const text = grid.join('');
  for (const ch of ['C', 'M', 'F']) {
    if (text.split(ch).length !== 2) return `'${ch}' must appear exactly once.`;
  }
  if (!Number.isInteger(catJump) || catJump < 1 || catJump > 8) return 'catJump is between 1 and 8.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(mouseJump) || mouseJump < 1 || mouseJump > 8) return 'mouseJump is between 1 and 8.';
  return null;
}

